                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "...Yeah, no, don't get The Complete Journey.\nIf you play every game in one single go, I don't know how good your experience may be, but the Save System is GENUINELY BEYOND BROKEN.\nThe Developer Commentary just stops working alltogether, some of the puzzles genuinely don't let you do them and then Skipping them does them WRONGLY SO YOU JUST GET SOFTLOCKED, some of the animations just stop working... For example, this all happened to me on the Pigeon puzzle! I can't see the pigeons, I can't do the puzzle, and skipping it makes Rufus do it poorly and then not let you edit it yourself so you're just softlocked forever.\nIt's genuinely sad considering this version is more economically efficient than buying the three games by themselves, have Chapter Select, Developer Commentary for all three games, etc. But THEY REFUSE TO UPDATE THIS VERSION TO FIX THE GAME.\nFor context, the three standalone games have gotten updates whereas this one got genuinely nothing to fix its bug, I've seen in some Discussion tabs people share save files that let you skip sections LOL.\nGenuinely just get the standalone games, I think they get discounts more often and you avoid risking a bug...\nIf you want to play this version though, just use the Chapter Select as your Save File system. You're forced to replay an entire chapter if you have to quit halfway but you avoid all the problems. (Of course, the collectathon achievements like Junkyard King and Pin-Point won't like it... But, you know...)",
